  "claim_boundaries": {
    "PROVED_LOCALLY": [
      "AR derives the independent low-pressure-output cost e_J(L) and transfers the same necessary signed work to high pressure outputs only when e_J(L) tends to zero. The diffusion-frequency choice leaves an unpaid sufficient A_J*Lambda_A cost, not a lower bound on actual pressure.",
      "AS retains the separated-input frequency ratio and a comparable-input half-order frequency moment. AT and AU prove only global and fixed-annulus local small-high-tail persistence, hence eventually non-small tails along legal large-L3 windows; common AO/AU thresholds require explicit redefinition. AV's fully corrected change of test returns the original cubic energy identity.",
      "AW.1-AW.34 derive the exact original Fourier pressure-work symbol, solenoidal contractions, phases, output denominator, zero-mode convention and nonlinear test coefficient. Only its particular pressure-side summation AW.29-AW.32 returns the earlier AS moment cost.",
      "AW.35-AW.44 prove that retaining the original test-output matching gives W_ang(chi,K,L)<=C_chi*(M^2*g^2+g^4), uniformly in K,L at fixed chi. The scalar absolute-coefficient field has the same H1 norm as h; coefficientwise domination and half-order Sobolev pairing justify the bound even with phases deleted.",
      "AX.1-AX.20 explicitly construct smooth real mean-zero divergence-free static Fourier fields with arbitrary fixed L2 energy E0 and uniformly bounded H1, while the actual high-pressure-output Fourier-l1 norm diverges at least c_*Q for every preassigned fixed K,L. All pairs in the protected output region have the same sign; low-mode energy completion does not alter that region."
    ],
    "LITERATURE": [
      "Sobolev and Hardy-Littlewood-Sobolev estimates are standard inputs, not new regularity results. The currently numbered Tao Corollary 46 was read with its kernel-exponent convention; the periodic adaptation by the mean-zero heat kernel and Riesz transforms is separately explained.",
      "The history record distinguishes actual full local source rereads, limited Tran-Yu primary-paper reading, and report-level deduplication of the already studied pressure moderator/conditional-expectation route. No exhaustive novelty search or full external-paper proof reaudit is claimed.",
      "Earlier pressure-regularity, local-smoothing and averaged-NS literature records are retained with their original assumptions and access boundaries. No transfer of every local pressure estimate or G to an averaged NS operator is asserted."
    ],
    "CONDITIONAL": [
      "All terminal-window statements preserve the original same-solution, fixed-data legal large-L3 sequence quantifiers, if such a sequence exists. No sequence or singularity is constructed.",
      "AW's normalized M^2*A_J/H_chi(t) cost is paid; H_chi(t)^(-1)*integral_[s_J,t] mu_J*g^4 remains unpaid. Its smallness is only sufficient for this absolute-value route, not a necessary condition for signed net-work control.",
      "AX only addresses pressure-side static Fourier-l1 and pairwise absolute costs. It does not prove pressure L-infinity or original test-work divergence, dynamic trajectory failure, or an AQ/G counterexample."
    ],
    "FINITE_COMPUTATION": [],
    "OPEN": [
      "An actual NS upper budget for the original weighted signed bad-time pressure work with negative 3*D_chi/4 retained",
      "Whether real time-ordered NS evolution improves AW's sufficient fourth-power gradient cost without unpaid critical-norm, endpoint-gradient or BV assumptions",
      "Original G/G-P/G-C moving shrinking geometry and actual NS generation of R.216-R.217; general regularity and the Clay problem"
    ],
    "NOT_CLAY": true,
    "novelty_claimed": false
  },
